+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of `add`,
+`remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) to a document and returns the result as a new
+value: neither `document` nor `patch` is mutated or shared with the result. Paths are JSON Pointers
+(`-` appends to an array in `add`). It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid (not an array, an
+operation that is not an object, an unknown `op`, a missing or non-string `path`/`from`, a missing `value`)
+or when an operation fails (target missing, bad array index, `move` into its own child, failed `test`,
+removing the whole document). `test` compares values structurally, with strict types.
